Fix ``unused-import`` false positives for names used only in the ``metaclass=``
argument of a class defined inside another class or inside a block such as an
``if``, or within a more complex expression like a conditional expression, a
call argument, a lambda or a comprehension. A name already used before such a
class is also no longer reported as ``undefined-variable`` when the metaclass
cannot be inferred. The names of a class body are no longer resolved from the
metaclass of a class defined in one of its methods, where they are not visible:
``undefined-variable`` is now reported for them, as for the bases.

Closes #1630
